					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SMOOTH\nThe smooth node smooths a signal over time. This is a great tool for smoothing big changes in a value. The signal gets smooth over the time input, this is in seconds. \n\nPatch Explained -\n\n• The Saw runs from 0 to 1 and then jumps back to 0.\n• The output of the saw affects the size of the red octagon.\n• The output also gets smoothed over 1 second before modulating the size of the blue octagon.\n• Because of the smoothing the blue octagon never really hits 0 or 1.\n"
					}
				},
